'' std/strings Format: every feature, every error code with its exact offset, and the argument
'' types tiko has (docs/tiko-strings/RFC-0002-format.md). The agreement with C++ std::format
'' is tools/fmtdiff's, run separately: it needs clang++ with <format>.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/std/format/format.tiko -o tests/std/format/format.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/std/format/format.exe
'' RUN: tests/std/format/format.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: format:  80 passed, 0 failed
